id: pm-rl-whrd
title: Train the bounded LM in external Compose jobs across recursive generations
description: "Reuse durable process ownership, reservations, receipts and recovery for bounded causal LM fits in isolated resource-limited containers; retain held-out evaluation and promotion in the controller."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: execution,llm-adapter,recursive-training
created_at: "2026-10-15T22:07:13.392Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T03:01:06.851Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Two real generations with successor collection; SIGKILL recovery, cancellation, corrupt checkpoint and limit refusals, one-launch contention; behavioural revert proofs and unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[24]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T22:07:43.111Z",codex-agent,"Design: extend the existing process contract with a typed LM payload and checkpoint validator; share owner fences, atomic reservation, staged adoption, cancellation and settlement. Keep held-out examples in the controller. Bind immutable image, memory and CPU ceilings into programme and job identity; send only frozen weights, source adapter, training strings and collected rewards to a networkless non-root container. Add real recursive generations and crash/cancellation/limit/contention drills, then behavioural revert proofs and unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-15T22:16:06.750Z",codex-agent,"First real Compose evidence: generation 1 checkpoint 058aa3d2c08438abd18cf0e9b455aca99ddb95492de852201c55c79a0672130d -> 37e503748a170be32e1d506997b6c0cc5c9ee256b24ab01fb49cf0564da07b4c; held-out sampled reward 0.183854, six steps, 1152 target tokens, observed wall 5567 ms, fit CPU 820 ms, peak RSS 138629120 bytes, retained staging 88930 bytes. Generation 2 collected with that promoted digest and trained -> 086f78992283cba37929321abe3961ca6132a52c332bf8a8387a52f22141cbdb; reward 0.292396, six steps, 1152 tokens, wall 5654 ms, CPU 803 ms, peak RSS 143323136 bytes, staging 92364 bytes. Both promoted through the existing gate. Real controller SIGKILL after completion before receipt commit recovered the same checkpoint and original reservation with one launch. Mid-fit cancellation retained input/events and process_cancelled. Full drills and coverage verification continue. The first linked run reached its default 120-second timeout; rerun will explicitly allow the complete integration duration."
  "2026-10-15T22:24:09.789Z",codex-agent,"Validated linked run: pm test pm-rl-whrd --run --progress --timeout 900 passed 8/8, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Real kernel memory drill retained partial allocation evidence and daemon oom_killed=true at 201326592 bytes; the time drill began the real 1000-step fit before exceeding its 15000 ms allowance. Both refused promotion and successor collection. Two-generation execution took 54134.161 ms; independent verification/replay/status took 4470.981 ms. Canonical hashes and held-out objectives match the first measurement. Final fit resources: generation 1 wall 4297 ms, CPU 713 ms, RSS 138207232 bytes, staging 89057 bytes; generation 2 wall 4266 ms, CPU 759 ms, RSS 144183296 bytes, staging 92509 bytes; both six steps and 1152 target tokens. Daemon receipts verify memory=268435456, CPU=1, no network and non-root user. Existing Compose barrier variability is tracked in pm-rl-8nev. Revert proofs and complete release gates remain in progress."
  "2026-10-15T22:29:39.962Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs in isolated source snapshots, unchanged tests: (1) restore only executePendingGeneration from origin/main, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real Compose LM promotes two\" test/lm-compose.test.ts: 0/1, no external process jobs. (2) Change only executeReservedProcessJob planned-branch guard to relaunch compose-lm running jobs, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real Compose LM staged completion\" test/lm-compose.test.ts: 0/1, exclusive staged input already exists instead of recovery. (3) Remove only the measured memory/token refusal in validateLmProcessCheckpoint, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"LM real fit publishes\" test/lm-compose.test.ts: 0/1, missing expected exception for invalid measured use. Restore those functions, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real Compose LM promotes two|real Compose LM staged completion|LM real fit publishes\" test/lm-compose.test.ts: 3/3, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. No live source, tests, thresholds or container memory ceilings were changed by the proofs."
  "2026-10-15T22:41:43.334Z",codex-agent,The first full npm release attempt reached the existing decision-recovery SIGKILL-at-every-HTTP-to-PM-boundary test and hit its unchanged 300000 ms timeout. The case is outside the authored LM path; baseline attribution and a complete passing retry are still required. No deadline or coverage threshold has been raised. Focused LM 8/8 and restored behavioural proofs 3/3 remain passed.
  "2026-10-15T23:04:35.050Z",codex-agent,"Gate follow-up pm-rl-bi4v now runs the two independent HTTP receipt datasets concurrently at each crash boundary, at most two scenarios active. No boundary, assertion, resource bound or test/coverage threshold changed. The paired covered case passed directly and through its PM-linked run (156944.936 ms, 1/1). This addresses the narrow serial timing margin observed in the first full release attempt. Complete fresh npm/Bun gates remain required."
  "2026-10-15T23:09:56.615Z",codex-agent,"Stopped the first, already-failed ordinary-temp release attempt after its recorded HTTP receipt timeout. Fresh full gates now use an isolated executable RAM-backed temporary tracker directory, with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration. Tests, all four 100% thresholds, source inventory, deadlines and container limits are unchanged. The separate ordinary-filesystem real Compose LM run and all eight real-container drills passed before this environment change; their measured evidence remains in docs/lm-adapter.md. Do not interpret the full RAM-temp gates as power-loss or physical-disk durability evidence."
  "2026-10-15T23:27:03.863Z",codex-agent,"The second full attempt exposed the existing orphan test startup barrier (pm-rl-8nev). Its final fix waits for the real running-job write and then starts the existing 15-second partial-artifact interval; the 30-second trainer allowance and recovery/accounting assertions remain. Direct covered and PM-linked checks pass. Image names and labels are unique per validation worker, allowing isolated npm/Bun gates without cross-worker image cleanup. The production trainer contract remains the implementation in ed4069c."
  "2026-10-16T00:15:16.855Z",codex-agent,"The remaining HTTP full-gate timeout was traced to SIGKILL fixture children inheriting coverage flags/raw-counter output plus the code checkout cwd. The built child now reports and enforces that it is uninstrumented and runs in its scratch project; parent source coverage stays unchanged. Focused explicit-raw-directory run passes all eight boundaries, PM-linked run passes inside 300 seconds, and removing only child coverage isolation fails on the runtime observation. Production LM code remains unchanged. Full gate restarts will be staggered so their long HTTP crash drills do not contend."
  "2026-10-16T00:28:06.054Z",codex-agent,"Additional receipt consistency regression: the pre-fix processLmTraining accepted a negative fit wall time, which participates in the combined generation deadline. An isolated pre-fix snapshot with the new assertions fails 0/1 (missing expected exception). Require fit wall >=0 and fit wall <= the completion process-wall measurement before evaluation. Both negative and larger-than-process durations are now refused as process_receipt_invalid. The fixed covered regression passes 1/1; normal measured fits remain valid. No resource allowance, deadline or threshold changed."
  "2026-10-16T00:31:03.675Z",codex-agent,"Fit-clock guard validation: covered direct regression and PM-linked --only-last run both pass 1/1 with zero skips. Explicit behavioural revert in an isolated source snapshot removes only the processLmTraining clock guard; the unchanged regression fails 0/1 with missing expected exception. Restore the guard and it passes 1/1. Valid canonical tensors and original usage remain unchanged; both negative and greater-than-reported fit durations refuse before evaluation."
  "2026-10-16T01:39:54.120Z",codex-agent,"Complete npm validation at df70cb0: all 590 tests pass, zero failed/cancelled/skipped. Line, branch and function coverage are 100%, but the unchanged statement gate correctly refuses 3977/3978 V8 blocks (99.97%). Raw counters identify the System One promotion-refusal null argument in executePendingGeneration. Extending the existing real-tracker terminal-refusal acceptance case across bandit and System One preserves every assertion and exercises compatibility with the shared LM lifecycle helper. The older Bun attempt was stopped before completion; it is not passing evidence. Both literal release gates will rerun after this coverage addition."
  "2026-10-16T01:42:49.046Z",codex-agent,"Coverage acceptance addition passes directly 1/1 in 18.475 seconds and through PM-linked execution 1/1 in 39.849 seconds, zero skips. Both real bandit and HTTP System One programmes exhaust one permitted promotion, keep terminal refusal stable, create no external job, make no replay query and refuse approval switching. Raw counters explicitly enter the missing null-argument block. Diagnostic union with the completed 590/590 run is 3979/3979 blocks across all 30 authored sources; this union is not a completed release gate. Production source is byte-identical to df70cb0. Typecheck, lint and changelog checks pass. Restarting both literal release gates at the new committed test tree."
  "2026-10-16T02:52:09.986Z",codex-agent,"At f405171 the completed npm attempt confirms all 8 new LM cases and the expanded System One compatibility case pass. Raw counters separately confirm 3979/3979 blocks across all 30 authored sources, with 100% line/branch/function coverage. The complete gate is rejected by the pre-existing packed CLI performance bound: 589/590 pass, measured 23890 ms versus 20000 ms. Reusing pm-rl-7c7m for exact evidence. An independent same-source Bun gate continues; a clean same-source npm validation checkout is prepared. This failed attempt and focused diagnostics are not gate approval."
  "2026-10-16T03:30:45.008Z",codex-agent,"Completed literal bun run release:check at f405171 in an isolated regular checkout: exit 0, 590/590 tests passed, zero failed/cancelled/skipped. Exact source inventory 30 files and unchanged statements/lines/branches/functions thresholds all 100.00%; 272 documented declarations; zero duplicate clones; approved identity audit; zero production vulnerabilities; packed contents 105 files; generated changelog current. Node 24.19.0, Bun 1.3.5. Full gate scratch trackers used isolated executable RAM storage and HOME/Git configuration; the separate measured PM-linked 8/8 Compose suite used ordinary filesystem storage. The fresh literal npm gate at the identical committed source/test tree continues. Earlier failed attempts are excluded from this completed gate result."
  "2026-10-16T03:47:16.337Z",codex-agent,"Final literal gates at source/test commit f405171 both exit 0: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 590/590 tests with zero failed/cancelled/skipped. All 30 authored sources meet unchanged statements/lines/branches/functions 100.00%; 272 declarations documented; zero duplicate clones and production vulnerabilities; identity, publish attestation, 105-file package and generated changelog pass. Node 24.19.0, npm 11.17.0, Bun 1.3.5. Separate regular checkouts use isolated HOME/Git configuration and executable RAM-backed scratch trackers. The ordinary-filesystem PM-linked 8/8 real-container evidence and resource table remain separately identified. Primary behavioural reverts fail 0/1 each and restored controls pass 3/3; fit-clock and child-coverage guards have additional 0/1 to 1/1 proofs. Cleanup verified zero owned containers and retained one task-built trainer image. Documentation/tracker-only receipts follow; source and tests remain byte-identical to this gated commit. Release configuration and dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-16T03:50:51.809Z",codex-agent,"Final metadata checks: strict PM health with required merge drivers exits 0 under CI-like isolated HOME; integrity and history drift checks are clean. Existing advisory storage findings remain preserved. The default user environment separately reports unrelated global extension/host skew, so no broad default-environment health claim is made. No dependency, global extension, telemetry setting or historical provenance was changed. Updated documentation packages successfully as the same 105-file distribution. Claims remain released and all items unclosed."
  "2026-10-16T04:19:43.232Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: fetched origin; main is already an ancestor of the existing PR head, with no merge needed. Read the complete failed Node 26 job log. Investigating the bandit Compose controller winner exit after 31 seconds, including IPC continuation and process deadlines, and comparing shared contention/accounting changes against main. Will preserve exactly one launch/reservation assertions, run 20 repetitions per available Node 22/26 runtime, and run both unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-16T04:27:13.125Z",codex-agent,"Investigation: full Node 26 CI log fails on winner exit code 1 after 31157 ms, not a duplicate-launch assertion. Main-to-PR comparison leaves controller lease acquisition/renewal, reservation accounting and the bandit launch path unchanged. Twenty diagnostic Node 26.7.0 repetitions passed before synchronization changes; original CI refusal is absent from that log, so its exact cause is not established. The test previously paused at collect before a job existed. It now pauses after the committed running reservation, verifies exactly one unsettled one-step reservation before trainer startup, and retains winner exit 0, one launch, one job, one history create and idempotent resume. Added refusal message diagnostics and exact-job cleanup on failure. No production code, resource allowance, lease duration, timeout or coverage threshold changed."
  "2026-10-16T04:27:17.535Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restoring only the original process-controller fixture with the new contention assertions retained fails deterministically at the reservation barrier (actual 0 jobs, expected 1; exit 1). Restored the fixture afterward. The new reservation state is therefore observable evidence rather than a scheduling delay. This proves the added synchronization invariant, not the historical CI timeout root cause."
  "2026-10-16T04:36:54.188Z",codex-agent,"Final unchanged-allowance contention loops: Node 22.23.1 passes 20/20 and Node 26.7.0 passes 20/20, zero failures or skips; each invocation executes the real Compose contention test. Independently checked all 40 reporter logs. The new linked contention command also passes through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress in the default schema context (1/1, exit 0). CI-style isolated HOME strict PM health with required merge drivers passes; default HOME separately reports the existing global pm-github version-skew gate failure and retained advisory findings. No global extension or history repair was performed. Next: full literal npm and Bun gates with isolated HOME/Git and executable RAM scratch trackers."
  "2026-10-16T05:51:23.733Z",codex-agent,"Extended CI parity: the failed GitHub job used Node 26.12.0, while initially installed Node 26 was 26.7.0. Installed the exact 26.12.0 runtime with verified download checksum. Three diagnostic original-source contention probes also passed on 26.12.0, so the historical refusal remains unconfirmed. The final synchronized test now independently passes 20/20 on each of Node 22.23.1, 26.7.0 and 26.12.0 (60/60, zero failures/skips). Re-fetched main; it remains an ancestor, so no merge is needed. Literal Bun release gate at source 91d40fc passes 590/590, zero failures/skips/cancellations, all four coverage dimensions 100% across 30 sources, 272 documented declarations, and all audit/package/changelog checks. First npm attempt retains 589/590 with only the packed CLI child reaching its unchanged 25000 ms timeout; concurrent diagnostic probes added load, so that attempt is not passing gate evidence. Serial npm retry is now running alone on exact CI Node 26.12.0."
  "2026-10-16T06:12:44.947Z",codex-agent,"Final local delivery at source/test commit 91d40fc: literal npm run release:check on Node 26.12.0 exits 0 with 590/590 passing, zero failed/skipped/cancelled, all four coverage dimensions 100% over all 30 sources, 272 documented declarations, and identity/audit/package/changelog checks passed. Literal bun run release:check on Node 26.7.0 and Bun 1.3.5 also exits 0 with 590/590 and the same unchanged four 100% thresholds. Packed CLI measured 10996.891 ms (npm retry) and 11086.851 ms (Bun). Preserve the first npm attempt: 589/590, sole unchanged 25000 ms packed CLI timeout; it is not passing gate evidence. Final contention loops are 20/20 each on Node 22.23.1, 26.7.0 and exact CI 26.12.0. The original CI winner refusal cannot be recovered from its log and did not reproduce; the reservation barrier invariant is proved, but the historical timeout root cause remains unconfirmed. Cleanup independently verifies zero repository Compose containers, and three owned validation images were removed after checking their exact owner label. Original history byte prefixes remain unchanged for both touched items. Main is already an ancestor; ready to push and wait for GitHub checks, without merging or resolving threads."
  "2026-10-18T03:01:05.676Z",codex-agent,"Audit: MET against recorded acceptance. Merged PR #80 (b255dfac6543ab178ab2720fad1de1ba49f91dd4) supplies two real external LM generations and successor collection, SIGKILL staged-completion recovery without retraining or double charge, cancellation, corrupt checkpoint and resource refusals, and one-launch contention. docs/lm-adapter.md and test/lm-compose.test.ts retain measured evidence; feature and fixture behavioural revert proofs are recorded. Final isolated npm and Bun release gates each passed 590/590 with exact four-metric 100% coverage. No acceptance gap found in merged evidence; storage kernel enforcement remains separately tracked in pm-rl-7073. Leave open for orchestrator verification."
